WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.800
We wondered when it would happen and it's
happening next week.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.700
Public hearings in Donald Trump's impeachment
inquiry are scheduled to start on Wednesday

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:09.700
now.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.019
There will be three witnesses to start.

00:00:11.019 --> 00:00:18.480
They will be William Taylor, the top us Envoy
to Ukraine, George Kent, a top state department

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:24.810
official and Marie over NAWIC, the former
ambassador to the Ukraine who says she was

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:29.460
told you'd better start tweeting positive
things about Donald Trump or you might lose

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:30.470
your job.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:35.110
We heard from the chair of the house intelligence
committee, democratic Congressman Adam Schiff

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:40.530
who tweeted yesterday quote next week the
house intelligence committee will hold its

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:45.380
first open hearings as part of the impeachment
inquiry on Wednesday November 13th we will

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:50.710
hear from William Taylor and George Kent on
Friday, November 15th we will hear from Marie

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:53.090
Yoav a NAWIC more to come.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:58.640
So the immediate question in general for this
impeachment inquiry is are the witnesses actually

00:00:58.640 --> 00:00:59.640
going to show up?

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.760
Now these three have already spoken privately
with investigators and there's every indication

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.290
they are going to be there.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:10.360
The real question is more about the other
witnesses that may be called and whether they

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:17.490
will be allowed to get away with simply ignoring
requests for documents, requests to appear

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.070
and potential subpoenas.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:23.730
So far they have shown that they are going
to try to avoid those and it's going to be

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:30.650
a question of whether Democrats try and or
are able to enforce those subpoenas that will

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.920
presumably subsequently be handed out.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:37.580
Now the format of these hearings is very interesting
and it's one of the most important elements

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:38.620
of all of this.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:41.640
If you've seen congressional hearings before,
you're probably used to, you know, you've

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:46.940
got 16 lawmakers who get five minutes each
with the witness and it leads to very little

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:47.940
substance.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:51.830
If you've got a lawmaker who doesn't want
to actually ask tough questions, they can

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:57.250
fill a Buster for four and a half of their
five minutes and then ask some dumb softball

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.250
question at the end.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.170
Like you would never do anything immoral,
would you mr witness?

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.170
No, I wouldn't.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:03.170
That's what I thought.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:04.170
Thank you.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.690
So that's one side.

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:09.000
The lawmakers who actually want to do the
work of questioning.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.520
The witnesses run out of time when all they
have is five, especially when the witnesses

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:18.940
can come prepared with techniques to not have
to answer questions and to consume a whole

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:20.330
bunch of time.

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:23.440
That is not how these impeachment care hearings
are going to go.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:24.440
Starting next week.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:29.750
The rules that were approved last week allow
Democrats and Republicans on the committee

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:33.510
to number one designate the questioning to
train staff.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:36.160
They can sort of delegate and say, I'm not
going to do the questioning.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.930
We're bringing in somebody who is actually
more specialized in this area, which will

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:48.080
be great, but more importantly, they will
get up to 45 minutes at a time of 45 minutes

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.300
at a time.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:54.370
Makes it much more difficult to avoid answering
questions than five minutes allows witnesses

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:55.850
to do so.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:57.170
That's going to be a very good thing.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:01.709
There's not that much more to say about the
hearings specifically until we get to them

00:03:01.709 --> 00:03:05.110
other than this is why voting matters.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:09.120
The 2018 midterms Democrats take over the
house.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.239
Okay, it's the house fine.

00:03:11.239 --> 00:03:15.610
We still can't get major legislation through
because there's a Republican Senate.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:19.980
Trump still controls the white house and could
veto anything that we get through a Republican

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:20.980
Senate.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:21.980
Who cares?

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:27.280
Well, we only have an impeachment inquiry
right now because Democrats won the 2018 midterms

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.020
and now control the house and the house intelligence
committee.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:36.709
If that impeachment inquiry is going to damage
Donald Trump and destroy his reelection chances

00:03:36.709 --> 00:03:39.020
in 2020 which it may do, it may not, but it
may.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:40.020
That's the goal.

